# zig-only
# Switching tab pages says where you landed once: `gT` / `gt` / `:tabnew`
# replace the previous `tab N/M` toast instead of stacking a new one, so
# after four moves only the last is on screen and there is no `+N more`.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
command editor.use_vim
ex tabnew
key g
key T
key g
key t
key g
key T
expect screen contains "tab 1/2"
expect screen lacks "tab 2/2"
expect screen lacks "more…"
